<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Movses Kaghankatvatsi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Movses Daskhurantsi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Movses Kaghankatvatsi is the name traditionally given to the author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/history-of-the-country-of-albania">History of the Country of Albania</a>, the main narrative source for Caucasian Albania. Written in Armenian, the work was probably compiled in the 10th century from older material, and its authorship, sometimes credited to Movses Daskhurantsi, is debated. It covers the conversion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a>, the Mihranid princes and above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javanshir">Javanshir</a>, together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> and Arab invasions.</p></div>
